{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Go and gather, etc.</b> The reason for the repetition of the matter a second time appears to be that HaShem intends to say that at the time of his coming to Egypt initially and first, he should say to every man of Israel that he comes as an emissary from HaShem to Israel, and afterwards he should gather all the elders of Israel together and declare to them his mission, blessed be He, for He has visited His people, etc." "And the reason for first informing everyone that he is an emissary to them from HaShem is so that by this means they will gather to him, for without this who would incline an ear to gather? Also, HaShem contrived to distinguish between things he would say to each and every man of Israel and things he would say in the assembly of elders, and the reason for the elders alone is for the sake of honor, as they of blessed memory said (Leviticus Rabbah 11:8): not one place, etc." "<b>Visiting, I have visited.</b> He said two visitations — corresponding to the visitation of the appointed end of redemption and corresponding to the visitation of them from their affliction. And that is His saying <b>etchem</b> (you) — corresponding to the end of redemption; <b>and that which is done to you</b> — corresponding to their affliction in Egypt, in order to redeem them from the affliction and bring them up to the land concerning which He swore. And He hinted to them that without that which was done to them in Egypt — which is the oppression, etc. — the time of the end has not yet arrived. Also, He hinted in saying <b>that which is done</b>, that He comes to exact retribution from the Egyptians for that which they already did to them."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:24:07.460383155Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}